return {
["01:00"]={"It was nearly \003one o’clock\004 when Sherlock Holmes returned from his excursion. He held in his hand a sheet of blue paper, scrawled over with notes and figures.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["01:01"]={"What time is it now? she said.\n“\003About one o’clock\004.”\n“In the morning?”\nHerera’s friend leered at her. “No, there’s a total eclipse of the sun.”","Freedom","Jonathan Franzen"},
["01:02"]={"Fallon approached the gat at \003two minutes past one\004, his swagger evidence of his satisfaction at the turn of events.","Blood Before Sunrise","Amanda Bonilla"},
["01:03"]={"Cleveland handed it to Toronto at \00301:03\004 EST; that’s seven minutes ago. At the moment, Toronto Center reports the aircraft’s position as near London, Ontario. I have more information — course, height, speed — if you want it.","Airport","Arthur Hailey"},
["01:06"]={"When he woke it was \0031:06\004 by the digital clock on the bedside table. He lay there looking at the ceiling, the raw glare of the vaporlamp outside bathing the bedroom in a cold and bluish light. Like a winter moon.","No Country for Old Men","Cormac McCarthy"},
["01:07"]={"\00301:07 GMT\004\nLamont could hear the sound of a car coming from behind him. Moments later a green Jaguar drove past and proceeded along the driveway, lights full on. It came to a halt outside the house.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["01:08"]={"My radio-alarm is glowing \00301:08\004 when I hear footsteps on the stairs, the pause, the timid knock-knock-knock on my outer door.","The Bone Clocks","David Mitchell"},
["01:09"]={"They made an unostentatious exit from their coach, finding themselves, when the express had rolled on into the west, upon a station platform in a foreign city at \003nine minutes past one\004 o’clock in the morning — but at length without their shadow.","The Black Bag","Louis Joseph Vance"},
["01:10"]={"February 26, Saturday — Richards went out \0031:10 am\004 and found it clearing a bit, so we got under way as soon as possible, which was 2:10a.m.","South: The Endurance Expedition","Ernest Shackleton"},
["01:11"]={"Declares one of the waiters was the worse for liquor, and that he was giving him a dressing down. Also that it was \003nearer to one than half past\004.","The Affair at the Victory Ball","Agatha Christie"},
["01:12"]={"That was under the pastoral cone of silence. Maybe I’ll be able to tell Jenn more at some point down the line. But not now.\nHe looked at the clock. It said \0031:12 AM\004.","Vatican Shadows","Ray Keating"},
["01:13"]={"He drew out his note-book and read aloud what the mysterious chandler had said to him: “It was precisely \003thirteen minutes past one\004 on the twenty-fourth of January when I drew my last breath.”","Atlantis","Gerhart Hauptmann"},
["01:14"]={"Sal is here, this is my old buddy from New Yor-r-k, this is his first night in Denver and it’s absolutely necessary for me to take him out and fix him up with a girl.\n“But what time will you be back?”\n“It is now,” (looking at his watch) “exactly \003one-fourteen\004.”","On the Road","Jack Kerouac"},
["01:15"]={"Lily Chen always prepared an ‘evening’ snack for her husband to consume on his return at \0031:15 am\004.","Sour Sweet","Timothy Mo"},
["01:16"]={"At \003sixteen past one\004, they walked into the interview room.","Nothing Gold Can Stay","Dana Stabenow"},
["01:17"]={"“I don’t know how you feel, but I’m exhausted,” said Ted, bolting the kitchen door.\nHazel checked her watch. It was \003seventeen minutes past one\004.","Shoeshine Boy","Jeffrey Archer"},
["01:18"]={"It was Saturday night, or technically Sunday morning. It was \003eighteen minutes past one\004.","Summerland","Elin Hilderbrand"},
["01:19"]={"Go to bed before he comes in, she ordered herself for the umpteenth time. Still, she sat looking at the clock. The minute hand had shifted to \003nineteen past one\004 and her nerves grew more on edge.","Haunted Husband","Elizabeth August"},
["01:21"]={"Friday \0031:21 A.M.\004\n“Your name Vance?” The Russian voice, with its uncertain English, was the last thing he’d expected.\n“Who are you?”\n“For this vehicle, I am Director Propulsion System,” he replied formally, and with pride, pulling at his white lab coat. “I must talk you. Please.”","Project Daedalus","Thomas Hoover"},
["01:22"]={"It was \0031:22\004 when we found Dad’s grave.","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer"},
["01:23"]={"Croydon Central was declared at \0031:23 a.m.\004, with a swing of 1.8 percent to the Conservatives.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["01:24"]={"Larkin had died at \0031:24 am\004, turning to the nurse who was with him, squeezing her hand, and saying faintly, ‘I am going to the inevitable.’","Body Parts: Essays on Life-Writing","Hermione Lee"},
["01:25"]={"He made a last effort; he tried to rise, and sank back. His head fell on the sofa cushions. It was then \003twenty-five minutes past one\004 o’clock.","The Moonstone","Wilkie Collins"},
["01:26"]={"When I reached the stop and got off, it was already \003one twenty-six A.M.\004 by the bus’s own clock. I had been gone over ten hours.","The Silver Metal Lover","Tanith Lee"},
["01:27"]={"It was a receipt for the purchase of 13.6 gallons of gas, a credit card transaction bearing Soderburg’s signature. It had been generated at the Food ’N Fuel at \0031:27 A.M.\004 on January 1.","Blood Hollow","William Kent Krueger"},
["01:29"]={"He exited the men’s room at \003one-twenty-nine A.M.\004","The Narc","William Edmund Butterworth"},
["01:30"]={"Around \0031:30 A.M.\004 the door opened and I thought it was Karla, but it was Bug, saying Karla and Laura had gone out for a stag night after they ran out of paint.","Microserfs","Douglas Coupland"},
["01:31"]={"It was \003one-thirty-one\004 in the morning. He poured another Crown. Downed it and repeated the process two more times.","Westerly","Michael E. Newell"},
["01:32"]={"She grinned at him with malicious playfulness, showing great square teeth, and then ran for the stairs. \003One-thirty-two\004. She thought that she heard a whistle blown and took the last three steps in one stride.","Stamboul Train","Graham Greene"},
["01:33"]={"He looked at his watch. \003One-thirty-three a.m.\004 He had been asleep on this bench for over an hour and a half.","Skeletons","Kat Fox"},
["01:34"]={"Myrtle couldn’t sleep. Her digital clock’s luminous numbers told her it was \00301:34\004 in the morning, which would be later than she had ever been awake in her life. But the questions were so many, and so insistent, that they just wouldn’t let her go.","Drowned Hopes","Donald E. Westlake"},
["01:35"]={"Two days later, the chime of his diary woke Merral in the middle of the night. He shook himself and peered at the clock on the diary screen.\n\003One thirty-five\004. An extraordinary time for a message. Has the ship been sighted?","The Dark Foundations","Chris Walley"},
["01:38"]={"At \003one-thirty-eight\004 am suspect left the Drive-In and drove to seven hundred and twenty three North Walnut, to the rear of the residence, and parked the car.","The Narc","William Edmund Butterworth"},
["01:39"]={"You are viewing the webjournal of blueeyedboy posting on: badguysrock@webjournal.com\nPosted at: \00301:39\004 on Friday, February 22\nStatus: public\nMood: nasty\nListening to: Gloria Gaynor: “I Will Survive”","Blueeyedboy","Joanne Harris"},
["01:40"]={"March twelfth, \003one-forty am\004, she leaves a group of drinking buddies to catch a bus home. She never makes it.","Bones to Ashes","Kathy Reichs"},
["01:42"]={"At \00301:42\004 and 26 seconds, the plane hit the side of Nimitz Hill, a densely vegetated mountain three miles southwest of the airport — $60 million and 212,000 kilograms of steel slamming into rocky ground at one hundred miles per hour.","Outliers: The Story of Success","Malcolm Gladwell"},
["01:43"]={"At \0031:43 a.m.\004 the cheers became louder when the Conservatives captured Basildon, which on Emma’s chart suggested a Conservative majority of around 30.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["01:44"]={"She knew it was the stress, two long days of stress, and she looked at her watch, \003sixteen minutes to two\004, and she almost leaped with fright, a shock wave rippling through her body, where had the time gone?","Trackers","Deon Meyer"},
["01:45"]={"In the end I accepted a glass of claret. It seemed both churlish and censorious to let him drink alone. The carriage-clock stuck \0031:45\004 before he roused himself and said: “Sorry, Cousin. Rather drunk. Be glad of your shoulder. To bed, to sleep, perchance to dream.”","The Mistletoe Murder","P.D. James"},
["01:47"]={"That night Cork woke, looked at the clock on the stand beside the bed — \0031:47 A.M.\004 — and realized he was alone.","Mercy Falls","William Kent Krueger"},
["01:48"]={"Mr. Peripart Sir then you immediately departed under a special clearance from the government at Saigon and returned here at \00301:48\004 local time.","Finity","John Barnes"},
["01:50"]={"No, she thought: every spinster legal secretary, bartender, and orthodontist had a cat or two—and she could not tolerate (not even as a lark, not even for a moment at \003ten minutes before two AM\004), embodying cliché.","Dog","Michelle Herman"},
["01:51"]={"At \003nine minutes to two\004 the other vehicle arrived. At first Milla didn’t believe her eyes: that shape, those markings.","Trackers","Deon Meyer"},
["01:52"]={"Link telepathically confirmed it was \003eight minutes to two\004 in the morning. I was only eight minutes away from the anomaly appearing again. The time in the 26th century was running out fast for me.","A Timeless Journey","Elliot Sacchi"},
["01:53"]={"Bony gave a further two swallows, retrieved the glass, told the old man to go to sleep, and left the room, walking without noise back to his bedroom window. He had been in his room only a minute when he heard the Buick returning. It was then \003seven minutes to two\004.","The Mountains Have a Secret","Arthur Upfield"},
["01:54"]={"\003Six minutes to two\004. Janina Mentz watched the screen, where the small program window flickered with files scrolling too fast to read, searching for the keyword.","Trackers","Dean Koontz"},
["01:55"]={"\0031:55 A.M.\004, Bayside, Queens\nTwo sets of stairs led to the basement apartment shared by Randall al-Hakim and Abdul ed-Din — one from the tiny backyard and the second from inside the home.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["01:56"]={"Mr. Peripart, Sir, at \00301:56\004 you ordered me back into shutdown mode.","Finity","John Barnes"},
["01:57"]={"Then I opened my eyes and looked at my watch. It was \003one fifty-seven\004. Twenty-five minutes had vanished somewhere. Not bad, I told myself. A pointless way of whittling away time. Not bad at all.","Blind Willow, Sleeping Woman","Haruki Murakami"},
["01:58"]={"It was \003two minutes to two\004. I checked my flashlight and envelope and let the inside of my arm touch the firmness of my holster through my jacket. It was reassuring.","Bullet for a Star","Stuart M. Kaminsky"},
["01:59"]={"For twenty minutes he sat and watched as the gap between the ship and Epun closed, as the ship’s computer teased and kneaded the numbers that would bring it into a loop around the little moon, and close the loop and keep it there, orbiting in perpetual obscurity. “\003One … fifty-nine\004 …”","So Long, and Thanks for All the Fish","Douglas Adams"},
